+Mounted on the real TableScreen: exact-event timeline and grouped transport,
+explicit arm/cancel/ordinary-action continuation, server-targeted Undo/Redo and
+explicit Redo route, compact group explorer, captured Make current, contextual
+archive/restore/worker-built exact return preview/recovery, event comments and
+card/player/area/occurrence pings, accepted-inspection observer, authorized activity
+boundary and result playback gate. Personal selection/camera and the common
+Canvas/gesture geometry are retained. Offline cached review is not blocked by a
+reconnect modal. Auth's existing sign-in/restore policy is unchanged; no offline
+authentication bypass or new mutation queue is introduced.
+
+## Material delta since kernel (fresh-verifier reconciliation)
+
+- `GameplayTree.prepareReview` primes **one** disposable selected endpoint on a
+  worker, not a per-node board map. Copies/decoding discard it. Selective work
+  ignores this memo and still reconstructs/charges tuples; the new focused
+  protocol regression passes. GameSession reviews call it before delivery.
+- GameSession sends shared controls without synchronous UI-thread selective
+  prediction. It does not wait for an earlier result; server-selected targets and
+  accepted worker deltas remain authoritative. Ordinary action prediction remains.
+- Review callbacks include the worker-derived opaque context version. Comments
+  and pings capture that version when available, never a hidden-data hash.
+- The existing typed ping registry now includes actual combat-area, combat
+  occurrence and Stack-effect IDs, without aliasing occurrences to source cards or
+  inventing a mixed LinkEndpoint model. Its protocol regressions pass.
+- AccountLocalData's retained handle is factored into the production
+  AccountStorageHandle. A real file-backed SQLite + GameSession test passes cold
+  accepted loading, offline review, same-driver binding, private clear and account
+  switch. JDBC test fixtures require the same foreign-key setting as production;
+  the initial missing setting and subsequent dependency-lock diagnostic remain red.
+- UI refinements fence inspector lifetime on historical-context changes, preserve
+  toolkit identity/camera while the index prepares, disable Continue until its exact
+  worker-reconstructed endpoint is ready, and require explicit restore for an
+  archived selection. Native source uses existing NativeUi.button readiness.
+
+`combined-affected-01` is the one initial combined invocation. Later commands
+exercise compile-blocked, failed, new or materially changed assertions only. They
+are an affected chronological union, **not** one green full-suite invocation.
+All observed failures and original JUnit bytes are retained. Final 06 and readiness
+07 pass. Native Compose/E2E tests are authored/compiled, never device-executed here.
+
+## Unchanged pending source owners and gates
+
+Occurrence **links** and indexed token search still need the supervisor's separate
+saved API pins. No evolving worktree, source alias, mixed endpoint or whole-catalog
+scan is consumed. The normal Ping mode submits only an identified existing target;
+empty-space coordinate creation is not guessed from screen pixels. Full native
+pointer/layout/rotation/notification/offline/restart journeys and location-ping UI
+qualification remain with I22/I31 and the supervisor's native owner.
+
+The AuthViewModel/AccountLocalData storage/privacy change requires materially
+affected earlier review reconciliation, not blanket B1/B2 recertification. Original
+runtime/lifecycle repairs and these later inputs need a separate fresh coherent
+verifier at the saved spine. B3–B8, final suites, policy and release gates remain.
+The unapproved returned-lobby starter policy is unchanged. No state/proposal/
+acceptance validators, application transitions, devices, deployment or paid work.
